@startuml
title S2 - Pick up: proposed interaction contract
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide footbox
actor Student
boundary UI
control Reservation
control Core
Student -> UI: Confirm pickup at origin
UI -> Reservation: reservation ID, origin, version, key
Reservation -> Core: Authenticated pickup intent
Core -> Core: Validate actor; deduplicate command
alt Exact replay
  Core --> Reservation: Original result / same Trip ID
else Fresh command
  group Serialize reservation, vehicle and source occupancy
    Core -> Core: Read current state and authoritative t
    alt Wrong owner / Hub or terminal state
      Core --> Reservation: Error; no pickup writes
    else Already Active with same pickup context
      Core --> Reservation: ALREADY_ACTIVE and existing Trip; no writes
    else Conflicting version
      Core --> Reservation: CONFLICT; no pickup writes
    else Confirmed and t >= hold_expires_at
      Core -> Core: Separate expiry transition:\nExpired; release claim; keep occupancy
      Core --> Reservation: EXPIRED; no Trip created
    else Confirmed but vehicle faulty / battery ineligible
      Core -> Core: Separate invalidation transition:\nCancelled; release claim; preserve occupancy\nCore keeps vehicle unavailable
      Core --> Reservation: RESOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
    else Confirmed, t < expiry, own Reserved vehicle eligible
      Core -> Core: Atomic pickup: Reservation Active; create unique Trip\nIN_PROGRESS, expected_return_at = t + planned duration\nVehicle InUse; clear Hub/space; free source occupancy\nPersist command result and event
      Core --> Reservation: Trip ID, pickup time, expected return, Active
    end
  end
end
Reservation --> UI: Result and authoritative state
UI --> Student: Trip started or specific recovery guidance
note over Reservation,Core
  Cancel / expiry / incident / pickup share the same serialization boundary.
  A failed pickup transaction leaves all pickup entities unchanged.
  The separately logged expiry or invalidation is not a partial pickup.
end note
@enduml
